      "message": "feat(build): sign the Inno-embedded uninstaller when a certificate is configured\n\ninstaller.ps1 asks sign.ps1 -Status whether CAMCRAFT_SIGN_* configures a\ncertificate. If so it passes /DSignToolName=camcraft, which turns on\nSignTool=camcraft and SignedUninstaller=yes in camcraft.iss, and defines\nthat sign tool as a sign.ps1 call (/Scamcraft=...), so ISCC signs the\nembedded uninstaller and the setup exe with the same signtool command and\ntimestamp server as the release exes. Without a certificate nothing is\npassed and the build is the unsigned one it was, named in the log.\n\nThe separate sign.ps1 pass on the setup exe in release.ps1 and\nrelease.yml is dropped (ISCC signs it now); release.yml's installer step\ngains the CAMCRAFT_SIGN_CERT_PASSWORD env it was missing.\n\nFixes #29\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
